12. IMPORTANT INTERVIEW POINTS

What is a loop?

A loop is used to repeatedly execute a block of code.

What are the two main loops in Python?

• for loop
• while loop

What is range()?

range() creates a range object representing a sequence of numbers.

Is the stop value included in range()?

No. The stop value is excluded.

What does iter() do?

iter() obtains an iterator from an iterable.

What does next() do?

next() retrieves the next value from an iterator.

What happens when an iterator has no more values?

It raises StopIteration.

Does the programmer manually call next() in a normal for loop?

No. The for loop internally obtains an iterator and repeatedly
requests the next value until the iterator is exhausted.


KEY TAKEAWAY

for loop → Repeats over an iterable
iter() → Creates an iterator
next() → Gets the next value
range() → Creates a sequence of numbers
StopIteration → Indicates that the iterator is exhausted